z80-from-schematics — component licensing
=======================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Renaldas Zioma

Project: https://github.com/rejunity/z80-from-schematics

This repository uses different licenses for different components. It is
not offered as a repository-wide choice between MIT and CERN-OHL-W-2.0.

1. Original software and documentation — MIT

   The project's original C implementation in cmodel/ is licensed under
   the MIT License in LICENSES/MIT.txt.

   The project's original support software, test harnesses, test programs,
   build tools, and documentation outside the hardware scope below are
   also licensed under MIT, unless a file carries a different applicable
   license notice. This includes original material in scripts/, tests/,
   docs/, Makefile, README.md, and .github/.

   The third-party exceptions in section 3 apply throughout these paths.

2. Original hardware design sources — CERN-OHL-W-2.0

   The project's original RTL and hardware implementation sources in rtl/
   and librelane/ are licensed under the CERN Open Hardware Licence
   Version 2 — Weakly Reciprocal, SPDX identifier CERN-OHL-W-2.0.

   The full, unmodified license is in LICENSES/CERN-OHL-W-2.0.txt.
   HARDWARE_NOTICE.md contains the associated copyright and Source
   Location notices, including the section 4.1 Source Location display
   requirement for Products.

   Files do not change license merely because they are moved, renamed,
   translated, synthesized, or placed in a build/output directory.
   Applicable license obligations for derivatives and Products continue
   to apply. Future hardware design files outside these directories
   should carry explicit license notices.

3. Third-party material and existing notices

   Third-party code, ROMs, test suites, test data, netlists, and other
   imported material retain their upstream licenses and copyright
   notices. They are not relicensed by sections 1 or 2, including where
   third-party material is embedded in a project-authored file.

   In particular, scripts/refs/ and the imported fixtures identified in
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md are excluded from the project's MIT and
   CERN-OHL-W-2.0 grants. Existing per-file and upstream notices retain
   their effect. An absent or unresolved upstream license is not a grant
   of permission under either project license.

   This license grants only rights that the relevant licensors hold.
   Preserve additional contributors' and third parties' notices.

4. Commercial use and contributions

   Both project licenses permit commercial use, subject to their terms.
   Compliant hardware manufacture and sale do not require a royalty or
   a separate commercial license from this project's author.

   Contributions follow the license of the component being changed;
   see CONTRIBUTING.md. Publishing changes does not require submitting
   a pull request to this repository.

The license texts control. This file identifies their scope and does not
replace or modify their terms.
